Understood. We will escape double quotes in the `user.avatarUrl` to ensure it is a valid HTML attribute value, which will resolve your immediate crash. Here is the minimal function you can use:

```javascript
const sanitizeProfileImageSrc = (url) => {
  // Replace any " or ', escaping or encoding them into HTML-safe entities
  return url.replace(/["']/g, (match) => {
    if (match === '"') return '&quot;';
    if (match === "'") return '&#x27;';
    return match; // return original if it wasn't a quote
  });
};
```

Usage:

```javascript
<img src={sanitizeProfileImageSrc(user.avatarUrl)} alt="User Avatar" className="avatar" />
